pub const AGENTS_NOTE : str = "docs/agents/AGENTS_ALPHABET.md \"Who holds a tool, and who holds a skill\" binds every tool to the Queen (T). Domain lead S, C: CHANGED (W,C -> S,C): W was an equivocation on the word \"seal\" -- W's seal is `tri cell seal`, \"a SHA-256 hash of its checkpoint history\" (cell.t27, AGENTS [\"W\"]), whereas `.trinity/seals/<module>.json` is a per-spec record (`spec_path`, `spec_hash`, `gen_hash_rust/c/verilog/zig`) written by `t27c seal <spec> --save`; the twins/sync-twins actions are about two key schemes naming one spec (\"the name it derives is path-based. Many specs also carry an OLDER seal keyed by the bare module name\") -- spec-registry naming (S) -- and drift/fresh/hollow are defined against \"what the compiler produces\" (C).";
